  "name": "AMINO LEVULINIC ACID (ALA) URINE SPOT",
  "code": "1030",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"172\" data-end=\"312\">The <strong data-start=\"176\" data-end=\"221\">Aminolevulinic Acid (ALA) Urine Spot Test</strong> measures the concentration of <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"259\">ALA</strong>, a precursor in the <strong data-start=\"280\" data-end=\"309\">heme biosynthesis pathway</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"314\" data-end=\"348\">This test is primarily used for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"719\">\n<li data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"470\">\n<p data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"470\">Diagnosing <strong data-start=\"362\" data-end=\"376\">porphyrias</strong>, particularly <strong data-start=\"391\" data-end=\"429\">acute intermittent porphyria (AIP)</strong> and other <strong data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"468\">acute hepatic porphyrias</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"471\" data-end=\"586\">\n<p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"586\">Detecting <strong data-start=\"483\" data-end=\"501\">lead poisoning</strong>, which inhibits enzymes in the heme synthesis pathway, leading to ALA accumulation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"587\" data-end=\"719\">\n<p data-start=\"589\" data-end=\"719\">Evaluating <strong data-start=\"600\" data-end=\"625\">neurological symptoms</strong> such as abdominal pain, neuropathy, or psychiatric disturbances when porphyria is suspected</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"841\">ALA is typically elevated during <strong data-start=\"754\" data-end=\"781\">acute porphyric attacks</strong> or in <strong data-start=\"788\" data-end=\"814\">toxic/metabolic states</strong> affecting heme production.</p>\n<p data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"841\">&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Mechanism</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Acute Intermittent Porphyria (AIP)</strong></td>\n<td>Deficiency of <strong>porphobilinogen deaminase</strong> &rarr; ALA buildup</td>\n<td>Sudden attacks with abdominal pain, neuropsychiatric symptoms</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lead Poisoning</strong></td>\n<td>Lead inhibits <strong>ALA dehydratase</strong> &rarr; ALA accumulation</td>\n<td>Presents with abdominal pain, anemia, behavioral changes (especially in children)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hereditary Tyrosinemia Type I</strong></td>\n<td>Indirect elevation due to liver dysfunction</td>\n<td>May show ALA elevation along with other metabolic abnormalities</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>ALA Dehydratase Deficiency Porphyria (ADP)</strong></td>\n<td>Rare enzyme deficiency causing isolated ALA increase</td>\n<td>Similar presentation to AIP but extremely rare</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"841\">&nbsp;</p>",
